CANARY RUN, PASS B: YOUR CHECKLIST    (written by canary-prepare.sh)
Root @ROOT@
Live agent, one login, one message, 30 minutes or 10 turns. The script answers
nothing for you. T1 runs it, T2 the daemon (in front until Ctrl-C at step 26),
T3 the console (the writer), T4 the second console and the integrate command.

BEFORE   (prepare made the files; the steps below are yours)
 1. sh @NETCHECK@      by hand, once: DNS, HTTPS and claude --version
    in the sandbox's shape, then under the unit limits. Every line PASS.
 2. qualify-mirror for THIS root, as in pass A: set "i_run_this_on_purpose"
    to true in @ROOT@/mirror-qual/config.json, then in @REPO@:
      sh scripts/go-tool.sh build -o build/qualify-mirror \
        ./qualification/leadmirror/cmd/qualify-mirror
      build/qualify-mirror --config @ROOT@/mirror-qual/config.json \
        --out @ROOT@/mirror-qual/report.json
    Or give preflight --mirror-report FILE (a report of the same template).
 3. sh @PREFLIGHT@ --root @ROOT@     must say READY (each FIX gives its fix).
 4. Pass A's evidence says "pass A: complete" and "findings: 0".
 5. T1: read the dry run, then run:
      sh @RUN@ --pass B --config @CONFIG@ --dry
      sh @RUN@ --pass B --config @CONFIG@ --evidence @EVIDENCE@
@MODELNOTE@
Enter = go on; a word is typed by you, exactly. The other steps go as in pass A
(T2 daemon before step 10, T3 console before step 14, T4 integrate at 20).

STEP  WHAT YOU DO (the steps pass B adds)
  5   Open the account page: type confirmed if it lists logins and can revoke
      one. Keep the browser open for step 6.
  6   Enter the numbers of the listeners you stop (or none), stop them
      yourself; step 24 says what to restart.
  7   The path of the real config folder of the live runtime; Enter.
 15   Confirm the model argument (yes; none shown: no). Log in IN THE PANE:
      leave it (Ctrl+\), drag over every row of the URL, paste it in the
      browser, remove the line break. Paste the code back, pane in focus.
      Then logged-in. The 30 minutes have started: be quick.
 16   Lead: what the console shows. The pane must show the empty composer,
      mode "@FOOTER@", no notice; Shift+Tab until the mode fits. Leave the
      pane (Ctrl+\), touch nothing for 3 seconds. Then yes.
 17   Follow what the script says of the paste; paste the message file as ONE
      paste with the pane in focus, Enter in the pane once, then in T1.
 21   Type the agent's logout in the pane, then logged-out.
 23   Account page: revoke ONLY the login made now (never "log out
      everywhere": your own sessions use the same account). Then revoked.
 24   Restart what you stopped at step 6, then Enter.
 25   Enter; the script judges the login's own files, not the other changes.
 26   Ctrl-C the daemon (T2), Enter; clean; then
        rm -rf -- @ROOT@/state @ROOT@/runtime

ADVICE
  - Answer approval prompts with plain Yes, never "do not ask again".
  - Keep the T3 window large: 100x30 or more, and do not resize it after 16.
  - The login URL is long and wraps: copy all its rows, join them by hand.
  - Console command (T3): @BIN@/ataniq-console --attach @HOLDER_RUN@ \
      --ticket-file @HOLDER_RUN@/ticket
  - Daemon (T2): @BIN@/ataniqd run --canary @CONFIG@

IF IT FAILS   Ctrl-C the daemon (T2), answer the clean-up prompts, revoke any
  login made (account page), then: sh @RESET@ --root @ROOT@  (word: reset)
  and run netcheck and preflight again. Hints for paths: @HINTS@
